{
  "id": "ss.enemy.worker",
  "name": "Worker",
  "description": "The nest's traffic — the one body on this roster that is simply an ant. That is the point of it: the Tracker is deliberately not an insect, one fused amber blob read as a shape and a glow, so the burrow's middle rank is drawn as the anatomy that one refuses. Three masses with real gaps between them, a pinched petiole you can see daylight through, and a head carried out in front on a neck rather than sunk into the shoulders — because three lobes in a row is a silhouette and a blob is not, and these two have to be told apart at four hundred on screen. The legs are kept thin and short for the same reason: fatten them and they merge into a mass under the body, which is exactly the read being avoided. Set wide and carrying low, because in the game this is the body that does not give ground when you hit it. Drawn facing +x, the game flips it. Gameplay radius 10.",
  "tags": ["ss-enemy", "worker"],
  "size": [32, 32],
  "meta": {"radius": 10},
